From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: ship licence files of bundled libraries

The wheels compile and ship FastJet (extern/fastjet-core, GPL-2.0-or-later),
SISCone (GPL-2.0-or-later) and the fastjet-contrib packages (each under
its own COPYING) as fastjet/lib64/*.so, and compile CGAL (GPL-3.0-or-later
/ LGPL-3.0-or-later) and Boost (BSL-1.0) headers into libfastjet, but
only carry the binding's own BSD-3-Clause LICENSE.

List the in-tree COPYING files, and widen LICENSE to LICENSE* so the
CGAL and Boost notices staged as LICENSE.<dep> at the project root
before the wheel build are packaged into dist-info/licenses/ too. The
sdist still only matches LICENSE at its root.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every fastjet wheel on PyPI, so it needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]
---
 pyproject.toml | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index ade2171..741d23d 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -11,7 +11,13 @@ dynamic = ["version"]
 requires-python = ">=3.10"
 readme = "README.md"
 license = "BSD-3-clause"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = [
+  "LICENSE*",
+  "extern/fastjet-core/COPYING",
+  "extern/fastjet-core/plugins/SISCone/siscone/COPYING",
+  "extern/fastjet-contrib/COPYING",
+  "extern/fastjet-contrib/*/COPYING",
+]
 classifiers = [
   "Development Status :: 1 - Planning",
   "Intended Audience :: Developers",
-- 
2.43.0

